## Engine invariants and execution rules

- Canonical session history is the durable source of truth. Active request context is a derived, budgeted view; optional compaction must never destroy or silently rewrite the canonical archive.
- Preserve complete tool-call/response structure, provider-native replay data, user constraints, and Stage 3 artifact references. Distinct calls remain distinct, including calls with identical arguments.
- Never invent model context limits, provider token counts, token prices, or cache behavior. Explicitly label unknown and estimated values.
- Work sequentially on branch work. Current inspected head: b38ea2161d288ce7b12d5be9ad1bb8bba7836295. Re-read this file, Agents.rst, current branch head, and target files before each stage. Update this TODO before substantive implementation and keep it limited to unresolved work.
- Do not merge, tag, release, or modify main without explicit instruction. No new branches. Production builds and verification follow Agents.rst.
- System-prompt changes are explicitly deferred. Do not modify prompt profiles or prompt behavior as part of these engine stages; count their request overhead only where needed.

